Bugfix: Fix `mount` refusing to mount when using `--repository-file`

Since restic 0.19.1, `mount` refused to mount with the error "mountpoint ... is
inside the local repository directory" when the repository was given with
`--repository-file` (or `RESTIC_REPOSITORY_FILE`) instead of `-r`, and the
mountpoint was below the current directory. The check that prevents mounting
inside a local repository ignored the repository file and treated the
repository as a local one in the current directory. It now reads the
repository location the same way as all other commands.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22025
